// Real per-language product name translations, keyed by the exact English
// `name` used in data/products.js. Applied automatically to every matching
// product by makeProduct() (see products.js) - so this is the single place
// to add/fix a translated name, no per-product wiring needed.
//
// This is a rolling effort across the ~870-product catalogue (see the
// conversation record) - entries are added category by category, starting
// with the highest-traffic ones (Indoor Plants, Outdoor Plants). A product
// with no entry here simply falls back to its English `name`
// (getLocalizedProductName in utils/localizedContent.js), same as before -
// never a blank or "undefined".
//
// Where a plant has a well-known common name in a language, that's used
// (e.g. Tulsi, Neem). Where it's a specific cultivar/hybrid with no
// distinct vernacular name (e.g. "Pink Princess Philodendron"), the
// genus/common part is translated and the cultivar descriptor is rendered
// in-script - the same approach Indian nurseries use on their own
// multilingual signage/catalogues.
